{"iter": 3, "id": "082fa66f", "parent_id": "fcb3faae", "operation": "improve", "status": "closed", "evidence_type": "not_significant", "code_dir": "C:\\Users\\Ray\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\candidate_082fa66f", "hypothesis": {"mechanism": "Because GAUC measures within-user positive-versus-negative ordering, replacing pointwise binary cross-entropy with uniformly sampled same-user BPR should improve GAUC enough to raise primary without changing the FM scoring function.", "success_criterion_paired": "Primary on val-tier-1 (the standard held-out validation split) improves by at least +0.0020 over the parent node's primary on val-tier-1, with GAUC improving by at least +0.0020 and nDCG@5 declining by no more than 0.0010.", "implementation_sketch": "Edit baseline.py only. Retain the existing k=16 FM, initialization, Adam optimizer, and prediction path. Sort training row indices by user_id once, identify users containing both labels, and create positive and negative index pools with user boundaries. Each epoch, sample positive rows globally and use vectorized NumPy indexing to sample one exposed long_view=0 row from the same user's negative interval. Compute FM scores for both arrays and minimize logaddexp(0, -(s_pos-s_neg)); derive the scalar gradient sigmoid(s_pos-s_neg)-1 and backpropagate it through the two FM forward passes with opposite signs, accumulating sparse parameter gradients using np.add.at or the baseline's existing indexed-update mechanism. Skip all-positive and all-negative users, sample roughly one pair per eligible positive per epoch, and test only a small learning-rate grid while keeping runtime below 240 seconds."}, "diagnosis": {"bottleneck": "The FM is optimized with pointwise log loss rather than a within-user ranking loss aligned with GAUC and nDCG@5.", "evidence": "The branch remains essentially at the plain-FM baseline, improving primary by only 0.00056, while the model is trained independently per impression even though both evaluation metrics depend on ordering candidates within each user; however, the history is too short to establish a definitive plateau.", "confidence": 0.66, "component": "loss_function", "edit_radius": "small", "expected_cost": "A localized baseline.py change implementing vectorized within-user BPR sampling or listwise softmax, with moderate effort for efficient grouping and batching under the runtime limit.", "incompatibilities": ["Independent pointwise-only minibatching that does not preserve or sample within-user comparisons", "Replacing the FM with train-only aggregate GBDT features"], "uncertainty": 0.34}, "per_seed_primary": {"0": 0.5958336591720581, "1": 0.5955508947372437, "2": 0.5958211421966553}, "per_seed_gauc": {"0": 0.6660842895507812, "1": 0.6654607653617859, "2": 0.6657467484474182}, "per_seed_ndcg5": {"0": 0.525583028793335, "1": 0.5256409645080566, "2": 0.5258954763412476}, "mean_delta": 0.00045983113028578423, "p_positive": 0.758, "lower_95": -0.0005077125634906065, "fix_attempts": 0, "wallclock_used_s": 0.0, "per_user_by_seed": {"0": {"4": 1.0, "15": 0.612025, "16": 1.0, "21": 0.340338, "23": 0.5, "25": 0.564817, "27": 0.679764, "29": 0.732132, "35": 1.0, "36": 1.0, "39": 1.0, "41": 0.83486, "45": 0.70986, "46": 0.590444, "49": 1.0, "50": 0.515361, "53": 0.298105, "54": 1.0, "55": 0.813608, "57": 1.0, "58": 0.801966, "60": 1.0, "64": 0.64856, "65": 0.527838, "67": 1.0, "68": 0.752965, "71": 0.340338, "73": 0.546037, "74": 1.0, "75": 0.817067, "79": 1.0, "81": 0.493007, "82": 0.786346, "83": 1.0, "84": 0.315465, "94": 0.315465, "95": 1.0, "97": 1.0, "98": 0.565465, "99": 0.565465, "102": 0.9, "110": 0.928178, "111": 0.34632, "112": 0.25, "113": 1.0, "114": 0.648798, "118": 0.786346, "121": 0.778514, "122": 0.826966, "124": 0.771941, "125": 0.577889, "127": 1.0, "129": 0.315465, "132": 0.45046, "138": 0.838608, "142": 0.731065, "147": 0.699748, "149": 0.66521, "150": 0.416667, "152": 0.294855, "153": 1.0, "157": 0.450633, "158": 1.0, "159": 0.346713, "160": 0.867731, "16