{"iter": 3, "id": "434bbc08", "parent_id": "fcb3faae", "operation": "improve", "status": "closed", "evidence_type": "not_significant", "code_dir": "C:\\Users\\Ray\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\candidate_434bbc08", "hypothesis": {"mechanism": "Because each user's candidates form a list and ordinary BPR treats every negative independently, a segmented within-user softmax loss with probability mass distributed uniformly over that user's positive rows should make positives compete jointly against all exposed negatives and improve both overall ordering and concentration of positives near the top five.", "success_criterion_paired": "Primary on val-tier-1 (the standard held-out validation split) improves by at least +0.0020 over the parent node's primary on val-tier-1, with nDCG@5 improving by at least +0.0015 and GAUC declining by no more than 0.0005 on the same tier.", "implementation_sketch": "Edit baseline.py only. Keep the FM scorer unchanged and sort mixed-label training rows by user_id once. Train on chunks containing complete user groups. For each chunk, compute all row scores, then use NumPy reduceat operations and repeated segment statistics to calculate a stable softmax separately within each user. Define the target distribution as long_view divided by that user's positive count and use gradient softmax_probability minus target_probability. Exclude zero-positive users from this loss and optionally exclude all-positive users because they provide no ranking contrast. Backpropagate the row-level score gradients through the existing vectorized FM gradient code and Adam optimizer. Cap very large user groups by uniformly subsampling at most a fixed number such as 64 exposed rows while retaining at least one positive, avoiding quadratic pairs, per-row Python loops, and score-dependent sorting."}, "diagnosis": {"bottleneck": "The FM is optimized with pointwise log loss rather than a within-user ranking loss aligned with GAUC and nDCG@5.", "evidence": "The branch remains essentially at the plain-FM baseline, improving primary by only 0.00056, while the model is trained independently per impression even though both evaluation metrics depend on ordering candidates within each user; however, the history is too short to establish a definitive plateau.", "confidence": 0.66, "component": "loss_function", "edit_radius": "small", "expected_cost": "A localized baseline.py change implementing vectorized within-user BPR sampling or listwise softmax, with moderate effort for efficient grouping and batching under the runtime limit.", "incompatibilities": ["Independent pointwise-only minibatching that does not preserve or sample within-user comparisons", "Replacing the FM with train-only aggregate GBDT features"], "uncertainty": 0.34}, "per_seed_primary": {"0": 0.5923978090286255, "1": 0.5916125178337097, "2": 0.5913686752319336}, "per_seed_gauc": {"0": 0.6606402397155762, "1": 0.6594944000244141, "2": 0.6596251726150513}, "per_seed_ndcg5": {"0": 0.52415531873703, "1": 0.5237306356430054, "2": 0.5231122374534607}, "mean_delta": -0.004358356098158008, "p_positive": 0.0, "lower_95": -0.006007049813352917, "fix_attempts": 0, "wallclock_used_s": 0.0, "per_user_by_seed": {"0": {"4": 1.0, "15": 0.67546, "16": 1.0, "21": 0.340338, "23": 0.340338, "25": 0.768007, "27": 0.679764, "29": 0.732132, "35": 1.0, "36": 1.0, "39": 1.0, "41": 0.45046, "45": 1.0, "46": 0.583981, "49": 1.0, "50": 0.14272, "53": 0.298105, "54": 1.0, "55": 0.63796, "57": 1.0, "58": 0.851064, "60": 1.0, "64": 0.753226, "65": 0.527838, "67": 1.0, "68": 0.752965, "71": 0.340338, "73": 0.476762, "74": 1.0, "75": 0.817067, "79": 1.0, "81": 0.33042, "82": 0.900401, "83": 1.0, "84": 0.315465, "94": 1.0, "95": 1.0, "97": 1.0, "98": 0.565465, "99": 0.565465, "102": 0.789466, "110": 1.0, "111": 0.403287, "112": 0.25, "113": 1.0, "114": 0.648798, "118": 0.786346, "121": 0.778514, "122": 0.826966, "124": 0.771941, "125": 0.769706, "127": 1.0, "129": 0.315465, "132": 0.83486, "138": 1.0, "142": 0.669328