{"iter": 4, "id": "682e4ebf", "parent_id": "fcb3faae", "operation": "improve", "status": "closed", "evidence_type": "failed_implementation", "code_dir": "C:\\Users\\Ray\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\candidate_fcb3faae", "hypothesis": {"mechanism": "Because GAUC is determined by within-user positive-negative ordering, replacing pointwise binary log-loss with pure within-user BPR logistic loss should improve GAUC and primary by making every update directly increase a long_view-positive video's score relative to an exposed negative from the same user.", "success_criterion_paired": "Primary on val-tier-2 improves by at least +0.0020 over the parent node's primary on val-tier-2, with GAUC improving by at least +0.0020 and total training-plus-scoring runtime remaining below 240 seconds.", "implementation_sketch": "Edit baseline.py only, adding a BPR training mode to run_fm while retaining the existing five-field FM and Adam optimizer. Once before training, stably sort training row indices by user_id and build compact arrays of negative row indices plus per-user negative segment offsets. For each epoch, select each eligible positive row once and sample one negative from its user's segment using vectorized NumPy random offsets; do not enumerate all pairs or loop over rows. Compute FM scores for positive and negative batches, let d = sigmoid(score_neg - score_pos), and backpropagate +d through the positive score and -d through the negative score, including L2 regularization. Accumulate gradients for repeated categorical IDs with np.add.at and apply Adam exactly as in the parent. Exclude users lacking either label from pair construction and initially reuse the parent's epochs, batch size, learning rate, initialization, and inference path."}, "diagnosis": {"bottleneck": "The FM is optimized with pointwise log-loss rather than a within-user ranking loss aligned with GAUC and nDCG@5.", "evidence": "The running best improved by only 0.00110 over the last three iterations and remains near the pointwise-FM baseline, indicating a plateau; meanwhile, both scored metrics depend exclusively on within-user ordering, which pointwise log-loss does not optimize directly.", "confidence": 0.72, "component": "loss_function", "edit_radius": "small", "expected_cost": "A localized baseline.py change implementing vectorized within-user BPR negative pairing or sampled listwise softmax, with moderate tuning under the CPU limit.", "incompatibilities": ["Continuing pointwise-only log-loss as the sole objective", "Replacing the FM with train-only aggregate LightGBM models"], "uncertainty": 0.28}, "per_seed_primary": {}, "per_seed_gauc": {}, "per_seed_ndcg5": {}, "mean_delta": null, "p_positive": null, "lower_95": null, "fix_attempts": 0, "wallclock_used_s": 0.0, "per_user_by_seed": {}, "seeds_run": [], "local_best_score": null, "n_visits": 0, "confirm_primary": null}
{"iter": 4, "id": "ba3bdb75", "parent_id": "fcb3faae", "operation": "improve", "status": "closed", "evidence_type": "not_significant", "code_dir": "C:\\Users\\Ray\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\candidate_ba3bdb75", "hypothesis": {"mechanism": "Because pure pairwise training discards all-positive and all-negative users and can provide unstable shared video and author estimates, a mixed objective combining within-user BPR with a smaller pointwise log-loss term should preserve global parameter calibration while making the dominant gradient ranking-aligned, improving primary more reliably than either objective alone.", "success_criterion_paired": "Primary on val-tier-2 improves by at least +0.0015 over the parent node's primary on val-tier-2, and neither GAUC nor nDCG@5 decreases by more than 0.0005 relative to that parent on the same tier.", "implementation_sketch": "Edit baseline.py only and add a hybrid mode to run_fm. Build and sample one uniform same-user negative per eligible positive using sorted NumPy index arrays as in vectorized BPR. In each optimizer step, compute the BPR gradient on the sampled pairs and a pointwise binary-log-loss gradient on a uniformly shuffled row batch, then combine them as 0.75 * mean_BPR + 0.25 * mean_pointwise before the existing Adam update. Normalize each component by its own example count so the mixing coefficient is stable across batches. Apply both components to the same FM parameters and regularize once per update. Test the fixed 0.75/0.25 blend first; only if it beats the parent but misses the paired threshold, compare 0.5/0.5 under the same validation tier and runtime cap."}, "diagnosis": {"bottleneck": "The FM is optimized with pointwise log-loss rather than a within-user ranking loss aligned with GAUC and nDCG@5.", "evidence": "The running best improved by only 0.00110 over the last three iterations and remains near the pointwise-FM baseline, indicating a plateau; meanwhile, both scored metrics depend exclusively on within-user ordering, which pointwise log-loss does not optimize directly.", "confidence": 0.72, "component": "loss_function", "edit_radius": "small", "expected_cost": "A localized baseline.py change implementing vectorized within-user BPR negative pairing or sampled listwise softmax, with moderate tuning under the CPU limit.", "incompatibilities": ["Continuing pointwise-only log-loss as the sole objective", "Replacing the FM with train-only aggregate LightGBM models"], "uncertainty": 0.28}, "per_seed_primary": {"0": 0.5951614379882812, "1": 0.5944920778274536, "2": 0.5940253734588623}, "per_seed_gauc": {"0": 0.6651325821876526, "1": 0.6643788814544678, "2": 0.6635746955871582}, "per_seed_ndcg5": {"0": 0.5251903533935547, "1": 0.5246052742004395, "2": 0.5244760513305664}, "mean_delta": -0.0012862489443730494, "p_positive": 0.032, "lower_95": -0.0024941933786181997, "fix_attempts": 0, "wallclock_used_s": 0.0, "per_user_by_seed": {"0": {"4": 1.0, "15": 0.443426, "16": 1.0, "21": 0.5, "23": 0.340338, "25": 0.564817, "27": 0.679764, "29": 0.732132, "35": 1.0, "36": 1.0, "39": 1.0, "41": 0.83486, "45": 1.0, "46": 0.55457, "49": 1.0, "50": 0.515361, "53": 0.253324, "54": 1.0, "55": 0.813608, "57": 1.0, "58": 0.851064, "60": 1.0, "64": 0.554044, "65": 0.527838, "67": 1.0, "68": 0.625, "71": 0.340338, "73": 0.649139, "74": 1.0, "75": 0.619679, "79": 1.0, "81": 0.493007, "82": 0.786346, "83": 1.0, "84": 0.315465, "94": 0.315465, "95": 1.0, "97": 1.0, "98": 0.565465, "99": 1.0, "102": 0.9125, "110": 0.928178, "111": 0.34632, "112": 0.25, "113": 0.876527, "114": 0.648798, "118": 0.786346, "121": 0.778514, "122": 0.826966, "124": 0.675172, "125": 0.67981, "127": 1.0, "129": 0.315465, "132": 0.688608, "138": 1.0, "142": 0.525117, "147": 0.841902, "149": 0.66521, "150": 0.416667, "152": 0.174202, "153": 1.0, "157": 0.168599, "158": 0.89736, "159": 0.70986, "160": 0.867731, "161": 1.0, "165": 1.0, "166": 0.408217, "168": 1.0, "169": 0.78268, "173": 0.732132, "176": 0.715465, "177": 0.315465, "17