{"iter": 4, "id": "62f79e6c", "parent_id": "fcb3faae", "operation": "improve", "status": "closed", "evidence_type": "not_significant", "code_dir": "C:\\Users\\Ray\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\candidate_62f79e6c", "hypothesis": {"mechanism": "Because unweighted BPR values every inversion equally and is only indirectly aligned with nDCG@5, a sampled within-user listwise softmax objective over one positive and several exposed negatives should concentrate gradient on high-scoring competing negatives, improving top-5 ordering and nDCG@5 without requiring full-list sorting.", "success_criterion_paired": "Primary on val-tier-2 improves by at least +0.0020 over the parent node's primary on val-tier-2, with nDCG@5 improving by at least +0.0025 and GAUC decreasing by no more than 0.0005 on that same tier.", "implementation_sketch": "Edit baseline.py only, adding a sampled-listwise mode to run_fm. Precompute contiguous per-user negative-index segments with NumPy sorting. Each epoch, take every eligible positive once and vectorially sample four same-user negatives with replacement, producing score arrays of shape [batch_size, 5]. Minimize cross-entropy where the positive occupies column zero: subtract the row maximum, exponentiate, normalize across the five candidates, and use softmax_probability minus one_hot_positive as the score gradient. Flatten the five candidate rows for the existing vectorized FM forward/backward routines, accumulate repeated feature-ID gradients with np.add.at, and update with Adam. Avoid Python loops over users or rows, full candidate-list softmax, and per-step ranking; retain the parent's initialization, regularization, inference, and early-stopping logic."}, "diagnosis": {"bottleneck": "The FM is optimized with pointwise log-loss rather than a within-user ranking loss aligned with GAUC and nDCG@5.", "evidence": "The running best improved by only 0.00110 over the last three iterations and remains near the pointwise-FM baseline, indicating a plateau; meanwhile, both scored metrics depend exclusively on within-user ordering, which pointwise log-loss does not optimize directly.", "confidence": 0.72, "component": "loss_function", "edit_radius": "small", "expected_cost": "A localized baseline.py change implementing vectorized within-user BPR negative pairing or sampled listwise softmax, with moderate tuning under the CPU limit.", "incompatibilities": ["Continuing pointwise-only log-loss as the sole objective", "Replacing the FM with train-only aggregate LightGBM models"], "uncertainty": 0.28}, "per_seed_primary": {"0": 0.5960352420806885, "1": 0.5959906578063965, "2": 0.5950648784637451}, "per_seed_gauc": {"0": 0.6666158437728882, "1": 0.6663697957992554, "2": 0.6653260588645935}, "per_seed_ndcg5": {"0": 0.525454580783844, "1": 0.5256115198135376, "2": 0.5248036980628967}, "mean_delta": 4.983997307386394e-06, "p_positive": 0.44, "lower_95": -0.0010041991004222507, "fix_attempts": 0, "wallclock_used_s": 0.0, "per_user_by_seed": {"0": {"4": 1.0, "15": 0.443426, "16": 1.0, "21": 0.340338, "23": 0.5, "25": 0.564817, "27": 0.718295, "29": 0.732132, "35": 1.0, "36": 1.0, "39": 1.0, "41": 0.596713, "45": 0.70986, "46": 0.480065, "49": 1.0, "50": 0.515361, "53": 0.284574, "54": 1.0, "55": 0.813608, "57": 1.0, "58": 0.748543, "60": 1.0, "64": 0.664185, "65": 0.527838, "67": 1.0, "68": 1.0, "71": 0.5, "73": 0.638009, "74": 1.0, "75": 0.817067, "79": 1.0, "81": 0.33042, "82": 0.786346, "83": 1.0, "84": 0.315465, "94": 0.315465, "95": 1.0, "97": 1.0, "98": 0.565465, "99": 1.0, "102": 0.834397, "110": 1.0, "111": 0.34632, "112": 0.25, "113": 0.876527, "114": 0.648798, "118": 0.786346, "121": 0.778514, "122": 0.826966, "124": 0.771941, "125": 0.653399, "127": 1.0, "129": 0.315465, "132": 0.45046, "138": 0.838608, "142": 0.721805, "147": 0.699748, "149": 0.66521, "150": 0.416667, "152": 0.205443, "153": 1.0, "157": 0.282034, "158": 1.0, "159": 0.346713, "160": 0.867731, "161": 1.0, "165": 1.0, "166": 0.527404, "168": 1.0, "169": 0.718626