{"iter": 5, "id": "3769a939", "parent_id": "fcb3faae", "operation": "improve", "status": "closed", "evidence_type": "not_significant", "code_dir": "C:\\Users\\Ray\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\candidate_3769a939", "hypothesis": {"mechanism": "Because GAUC measures positive-negative ordering within each user, replacing pointwise binary cross-entropy with uniformly sampled within-user BPR should direct every useful gradient toward the evaluated ordering and improve GAUC without spending capacity on user-constant calibration.", "success_criterion_paired": "On val-tier-1, the pure-BPR candidate's primary improves by at least +0.0020 over the parent pointwise FM's primary on the same tier, with GAUC improving by at least +0.0020 and nDCG@5 declining by no more than 0.0010.", "implementation_sketch": "Edit baseline.py only, retaining the existing five-field FM, k=16 parameters, Adam optimizer, and scorer. Sort negative row indices by encoded user once; build per-user negative-pool starts and counts, then map each eligible positive row to one negative from the same user using vectorized random offsets. Exclude users lacking either label and resample one negative per positive each epoch. Compute positive and negative FM scores in vectorized batches and minimize mean logaddexp(0, -(score_pos-score_neg))); backpropagate the score-difference gradients through both FM passes and accumulate shared feature gradients with the existing NumPy machinery. Sweep only learning rates {0.5x, 1.0x} of the parent setting and pair ratios {1, 2} negatives per positive, selecting solely on val-tier-1 primary. Never materialize all positive-negative pairs or loop over rows."}, "diagnosis": {"bottleneck": "The FM is optimized with pointwise logloss rather than a within-user ranking loss aligned with GAUC and nDCG@5.", "evidence": "The running best has plateaued at 0.595735, with only 0.000537 improvement over the last three-iteration window, suggesting further tuning of the existing pointwise FM is unlikely to help; pairwise BPR or within-user softmax remains unexplored and directly targets candidate ordering.", "confidence": 0.72, "component": "loss_function", "edit_radius": "small", "expected_cost": "A localized baseline.py change implementing vectorized within-user pair sampling and a BPR loss, followed by a small validation sweep over sampling ratio and learning rate.", "incompatibilities": ["Continuing to use pointwise binary cross-entropy as the sole training objective", "Sampling pairs across different users"], "uncertainty": 0.34}, "per_seed_primary": {"0": 0.5962722301483154, "1": 0.5965419411659241, "2": 0.5954760313034058}, "per_seed_gauc": {"0": 0.6670584082603455, "1": 0.6670489311218262, "2": 0.6656083464622498}, "per_seed_ndcg5": {"0": 0.5254861116409302, "1": 0.526034951210022, "2": 0.525343656539917}, "mean_delta": 0.000800147879566734, "p_positive": 0.908, "lower_95": -0.00015140184199253416, "fix_attempts": 0, "wallclock_used_s": 0.0, "per_user_by_seed": {"0": {"4": 1.0, "15": 0.443426, "16": 1.0, "21": 0.340338, "23": 0.5, "25": 0.539817, "27": 0.751849, "29": 0.732132, "35": 1.0, "36": 1.0, "39": 1.0, "41": 0.596713, "45": 0.70986, "46": 0.640773, "49": 1.0, "50": 0.515361, "53": 0.329355, "54": 1.0, "55": 0.813608, "57": 1.0, "58": 0.851064, "60": 1.0, "64": 0.736224, "65": 0.527838, "67": 1.0, "68": 0.752965, "71": 0.340338, "73": 0.678774, "74": 1.0, "75": 0.817067, "79": 1.0, "81": 0.61521, "82": 0.616414, "83": 1.0, "84": 0.315465, "94": 0.315465, "95": 1.0, "97": 1.0, "98": 0.565465, "99": 1.0, "102": 0.9, "110": 1.0, "111": 0.34632, "112": 0.25, "113": 1.0, "114": 0.648798, "118": 0.786346, "121": 0.778514, "122": 0.826966, "124": 0.771941, "125": 0.667785, "127": 1.0, "129": 0.315465, "132": 0.45046, "138": 0.838608, "142": 0.740324, "147": 0.841902, "149": 0.66521, "150": 0.416667, "152": 0.220215, "153": 1.0, "157": 0.232034, "158": 1.0, "159": 0.346713, "160": 0.867731, "161": 1.0, "165": 1.0, "166": 0.469973, "168": 1.0, "169": 0.