{"iter": 5, "id": "758f527f", "parent_id": "fcb3faae", "operation": "improve", "status": "closed", "evidence_type": "not_significant", "code_dir": "C:\\Users\\Ray\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\candidate_758f527f", "hypothesis": {"mechanism": "Because exposed-video long_view labels are noisy and unweighted BPR may sacrifice top-five quality, a mixed objective dominated by within-user BPR but regularized by a small pointwise logloss term should preserve the parent FM's calibration and nDCG@5 while adding ranking-aligned gradients that improve GAUC.", "success_criterion_paired": "On val-tier-1, the mixed-loss candidate's primary improves by at least +0.0025 over the parent pointwise FM's primary on the same tier, and neither GAUC nor nDCG@5 decreases relative to that parent.", "implementation_sketch": "Edit baseline.py only. Add the same vectorized same-user positive-negative sampler as for BPR, but optimize L = alpha*L_BPR + (1-alpha)*L_BCE, where BCE is evaluated on a vectorized balanced batch containing the sampled positive and negative rows. Test alpha in {0.75, 0.9}; use one freshly sampled within-user negative per positive per epoch and keep the parent's FM architecture, initialization, regularization, and Adam implementation unchanged. Combine the two analytic score gradients before the existing parameter update so runtime remains a small constant multiple of the baseline. Use val-tier-1 primary to choose alpha and learning rate, with no hidden-test iteration."}, "diagnosis": {"bottleneck": "The FM is optimized with pointwise logloss rather than a within-user ranking loss aligned with GAUC and nDCG@5.", "evidence": "The running best has plateaued at 0.595735, with only 0.000537 improvement over the last three-iteration window, suggesting further tuning of the existing pointwise FM is unlikely to help; pairwise BPR or within-user softmax remains unexplored and directly targets candidate ordering.", "confidence": 0.72, "component": "loss_function", "edit_radius": "small"