{"iter": 5, "id": "74b64c5c", "parent_id": "fcb3faae", "operation": "improve", "status": "closed", "evidence_type": "not_significant", "code_dir": "C:\\Users\\Ray\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\candidate_74b64c5c", "hypothesis": {"mechanism": "Because ordinary BPR weights bottom-of-list inversions as strongly as swaps affecting the first five positions, weighting sampled within-user positive-negative pairs by their approximate change in nDCG@5 and emphasizing currently high-scoring negatives should concentrate learning on errors that affect the primary metric's top-five component.", "success_criterion_paired": "On val-tier-1, the nDCG-weighted pairwise candidate's primary improves by at least +0.0020 over the parent pure-BPR candidate's primary on the same tier, with nDCG@5 improving by at least +0.0030 and GAUC declining by no more than 0.0010.", "implementation_sketch": "Edit baseline.py only and use this as a conditional child after pure BPR. At the start of each epoch, score all training rows once, obtain within-user ranks with a single np.lexsort over user code and negative score, and compute per-user IDCG@5 from positive counts. For each positive anchor, sample three negatives from that user's contiguous negative pool using vectorized offsets and retain the highest-scoring sampled negative. Weight its BPR loss by abs(D(rank_pos)-D(rank_neg))/IDCG, where D(r)=1/log2(r+2) for zero-based ranks below 5 and 0 otherwise; add a small floor such as 0.1 times the ordinary BPR weight so GAUC-relevant pairs outside the top five still train. Normalize weights to mean one and reuse the existing vectorized FM gradient and Adam update. Compare weight floors {0.05, 0.1} on val-tier-1; do not sort per batch or enumerate all pairs."}, "diagnosis": {"bottleneck": "The FM is optimized with pointwise logloss rather than a within-user ranking loss aligned with GAUC and nDCG@5.", "evidence": "The running best has plateaued at 0.595735, with only 0.000537 improvement over the last three-iteration window, suggesting further tuning of the existing pointwise FM is unlikely to help; pairwise BPR or within-user softmax remains unexplored and directly targets candidate ordering.", "confidence": 0.72, "component": "loss_function", "edit_radius": "small", "expected_cost": "A localized baseline.py change implementing vectorized within-user pair sampling and a BPR loss, followed by a small validation sweep over sampling ratio and learning rate.", "incompatibilities": ["Continuing to use pointwise binary cross-entropy as the sole training objective", "Sampling pairs across different users"], "uncertainty": 0.34}, "per_seed_primary": {"0": 0.5853586792945862, "1": 0.5831246376037598, "2": 0.584901750087738}, "per_seed_gauc": {"0": 0.6507534384727478, "1": 0.646775484085083, "2": 0.6497417092323303}, "per_seed_ndcg5": {"0": 0.5199639201164246, "1": 0.5194738507270813, "2": 0.5200617909431458}, "mean_delta": -0.013552095190012851, "p_positive": 0.0, "lower_95": -0.01544335778104155, "fix_attempts": 0, "wallclock_used_s": 0.0, "per_user_by_seed": {"0": {"4": 1.0, "15": 0.606574, "16": 1.0, "21": 0.690465, "23": 0.690465, "25": 0.65542, "27": 0.668341, "29": 0.732132, "35": 1.0, "36": 1.0, "39": 1.0, "41": 0.45046, "45": 1.0, "46": 0.444191, "49": 0.841902, "50": 0.38504, "53": 0.507169, "54": 1.0, "55": 0.737672, "57": 1.0, "58": 0.801966, "60": 0.315465, "64": 0.509784, "65": 0.527838, "67": 1.0, "68": 0.752965, "71": 0.340338, "73": 0.450393, "74": 1.0, "75": 0.817067, "79": 1.0, "81": 0.726966, "82": 0.616414, "83": 1.0, "84": 0.315465, "94": 1.0, "95": 1.0, "97": 1.0, "98": 1.0, "99": 1.0, "102": 0.9375, "110": 0.699748, "111": 0.071429, "112": 0.25, "113": 1.0, "114": 1.0, "118": 0.616414, "121": 0.685292, "122": 1.0, "124": 0.771941, "125": 0.761152, "127": 1.0, "129": 1.0, "132": 0.83486, "138": 1.0, "142": 0.474467, "147": 0.699748, "149": 0.60134, "150": 0.416667, "152": 0.592325, "153": 1.0, "157": 0.0, "158": 1.0, "159": 1.0, "160": 0.748543, "161": 1.0, "