{"iter": 6, "id": "21a6e2b5", "parent_id": "5b7ba11d", "operation": "improve", "status": "open", "evidence_type": null, "code_dir": "C:\\Users\\Ray\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\candidate_21a6e2b5", "hypothesis": {"mechanism": "Because GAUC measures same-user positive-negative ordering, replacing independent pointwise log-loss with same-user pairwise logistic BPR loss should directly reduce the inversions counted by GAUC; user-constant terms cancel from score differences while user-video and user-context interactions receive ranking-aligned gradients.", "success_criterion_paired": "Primary on val-tier-1 improves by at least +0.0020 over the parent node's primary on val-tier-1, with GAUC improving by at least +0.0015 and nDCG@5 decreasing by no more than 0.0005 on the same tier.", "implementation_sketch": "Edit baseline.py only. Keep the existing k=16 FM scorer, parameters, Adam optimizer, and inference path. Precompute mixed-label user groups using NumPy sorting, bincount, and group offsets. At each epoch, generate one pair per positive row by vectorized uniform sampling from that user's exposed negative rows. For each batch compute d = score_positive - score_negative and loss = logaddexp(0, -d), then backpropagate the sigmoid(-d) gradient through both FM scores with opposite signs using indexed NumPy accumulation. Exclude all-positive and all-negative users and keep the original epoch count initially."}, "diagnosis": {"bottleneck": "The FM is bottlenecked by its pointwise log-loss objective, which does not directly optimize within-user ranking.", "evidence": "The running best has nearly plateaued, improving only 0.00090 over the last three-iteration window, while the model is still trained pointwise despite GAUC and nDCG@5 depending entirely on within-user ordering; no evidence indicates that pairwise or listwise FM losses have been tested.", "confidence": 0.72, "component": "loss_function", "edit_radius": "small", "expected_cost": "A localized baseline.py change implementing vectorized within-user BPR negative pairing or grouped softmax, followed by validation of sampling and learning-rate settings; feasible within the CPU budget.", "incompatibilities": ["Continuing to optimize only independent per-row pointwise log-loss", "Sampling negatives without preserving within-user comparisons"], "uncertainty": 0.28}, "per_seed_primary": {"0": 0.595856785774231, "1": 0.5945397615432739, "2": 0.5950406789779663}, "per_seed_gauc": {"0": 0.6660932898521423, "1": 0.6640611290931702, "2": 0.6649154424667358}, "per_seed_ndcg5": {"0": 0.5256203413009644, "1": 0.5250184535980225, "2": 0.5251659750938416}, "mean_delta": 0.0013836244721865247, "p_positive": 0.962, "lower_95": 0.00011371452175509455, "fix_attempts": 0, "wallclock_used_s": 0.0, "per_user_by_seed": {"0": {"4": 1.0, "15": 0.612025, "16": 1.0, "21": 0.5, "23": 0.340338, "25": 0.539817, "27": 0.679764, "29": 0.732132, "35": 1.0, "36": 1.0, "39": 1.0, "41": 0.596713, "45": 1.0, "46": 0.621165, "49": 1.0, "50": 0.643626, "53": 0.284574, "54": 1.0, "55": 0.813608, "57": 1.0, "58": 0.801966, "60": 1.0, "64": 0.50409, "65": 0.527838, "67": 1.0, "68": 1.0, "71": 0.5, "73": 0.56824, "74": 1.0, "75": 0.817067, "79": 0.648798, "81": 0.61521, "82": 0.616414, "83": 1.0, "84": 0.315465, "94": 0.315465, "95": 1.0, "97": 1.0, "98": 0.565465, "99": 1.0, "102": 0.9375, "110": 1.0, "111": 0.479141, "112": 0.25, "113": 1.0, "114": 0.648798, "118": 0.786346, "121": 0.778514, "122": 0.826966, "124": 0.771941, "125": 0.667785, "127": 1.0, "129": 0.315465, "132": 0.688608, "138": 0.90986, "142": 0.731065, "147": 0.699748, "149": 0.66521, "150": 0.416667, "152": 0.287021, "153": 1.0, "157": 0.282034, "158": 1.0, "159": 0.346713, "160": 0.867731, "161": 1.0, "165": 1.0, "166": 0.542176, "168": 1.0, "169": 0.793131, "173": 0.583333, "176": 1.0, "177": 0.315465, "179": 0.884397, "187": 0.565465, "191": 1.0, "192": 1.0, "198": 0.55, "204": 0.611783, "209": 1.0, "210": 0.818326, "211": 0.535321, "212": 1.0, "213": 0.