{"iter": 7, "id": "0a85759f", "parent_id": "bbe18131", "operation": "improve", "status": "closed", "evidence_type": "not_significant", "code_dir": "C:\\Users\\Ray\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\candidate_0a85759f", "hypothesis": {"mechanism": "Because GAUC is the positive-negative ordering accuracy within each eligible user, replacing most of the FM's independent pointwise loss with within-user BPR should directly reduce ranking inversions; retaining a small pointwise term should stabilize training and prevent severe score drift.", "success_criterion_paired": "Primary on val-tier-2 improves by at least +0.0020 over the parent node's primary on val-tier-2, with GAUC changing by at least +0.0010 and nDCG@5 not decreasing by more than 0.0005 on that same tier.", "implementation_sketch": "Edit baseline.py only. Add a mixed-loss mode to run_fm. Once before training, sort row indices by user_id and build contiguous positive and negative index pools with per-user offsets for users having both labels. For each vectorized pair minibatch, sample 50% of users uniformly over eligible users and 50% in proportion to positive count, then sample one positive and one negative row from each selected user's pools. Compute FM scores s_pos and s_neg and optimize 0.8 times softplus(-(s_pos-s_neg)) plus 0.2 times the existing pointwise logistic loss on the paired rows. Accumulate opposite pairwise score gradients through the existing vectorized FM gradient and Adam update. Use a fixed number of sampled pairs approximately equal to the number of training rows per epoch, test pairwise weights 0.6 and 0.8 on validation, and retain the existing prediction path."}, "diagnosis": {"bottleneck": "The FM's pointwise log-loss is mismatched to the within-user ranking metrics, leaving relative positive-versus-negative ordering under-optimized.", "evidence": "The running-best primary has plateaued at 0.59610, with only 0.00036 improvement over the last three iterations, while the current FM still optimizes independent row probabilities rather than GAUC and nDCG ordering within each user. This suggests further tuning of the same pointwise setup has limited headroom.", "confidence": 0.78, "component": "loss_function", "edit_radius": "small", "expected_cost": "A localized baseline.py change implementing vectorized within-user BPR negative pairing or sampled listwise softmax, followed by validation of sampling ratio and loss mixing; feasible on one CPU within the runtime budget.", "incompatibilities": ["Keeping pure pointwise log-loss as the sole training objective", "Generating all positive-negative pairs per user, which would exceed the runtime budget"], "uncertainty": 0.28, "audit_concerns": ["test_label_access: ysel from enc[select_on] is read by evaluate() for model selection, and the diff does not establish that select_on cannot be the test split; this is safe only if select_on is always a labeled validation split."]}, "per_seed_primary": {"0": 0.5937131643295288, "1": 0.5938398838043213, "2": 0.5943408012390137}, "per_seed_gauc": {"0": 0.6629980206489563, "1": 0.6629848480224609, "2": 0.6638363599777222}, "per_seed_ndcg5": {"0": 0.5244283676147461, "1": 0.5246949791908264, "2": 0.52484530210495}, "mean_delta": -0.002165562756257267, "p_positive": 0.002, "lower_95": -0.0032488161373232976, "fix_attempts": 0, "wallclock_used_s": 0.0, "per_user_by_seed": {"0": {"4": 1.0, "15": 0.443426, "16": 1.0, "21": 0.340338, "23": 0.5, "25": 0.507386, "27": 0.718295, "29": 0.732132, "35": 1.0, "36": 1.0, "39": 1.0, "41": 0.45046, "45": 0.70986, "46": 0.530394, "49": 1.0, "50": 0.515361, "53": 0.329355, "54": 1.0, "55": 0.63796, "57": 1.0, "58": 0.801966, "60": 1.0, "64": 0.777405, "65": 0.527838, "67": 1.0, "68": 1.0, "71": 0.340338, "73": 0.517614, "74": 1.0, "75": 0.817067, "79": 0.648798, "81": 0.726966, "82": 0.786346, "83": 1.0, "84": 0.315465, "94": 1.0, "95": 1.0, "97": 1.0, "98": 0.565465, "99": 1.0, "102": 0.859397, "110": 0.928178, "111": 0.403287, "112": 0.25, "113": 0.8