{"iter": 7, "id": "361ff303", "parent_id": "bbe18131", "operation": "improve", "status": "closed", "evidence_type": "not_significant", "code_dir": "C:\\Users\\Ray\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\candidate_361ff303", "hypothesis": {"mechanism": "Because ordinary BPR spends equal effort on already-easy negatives far below the top five, selecting a moderately hard displayed negative from a small within-user sample should concentrate FM updates on inversions most likely to affect nDCG@5 while still improving positive-negative ordering for GAUC.", "success_criterion_paired": "Primary on val-tier-2 improves by at least +0.0020 over the parent node's primary on val-tier-2, with nDCG@5 improving by at least +0.0015 and GAUC not decreasing by more than 0.0005 on that same tier.", "implementation_sketch": "Edit baseline.py only. Reuse NumPy-sorted per-user positive and negative pools in a new hard-negative BPR mode in run_fm. Sample eligible users with the same 50% uniform and 50% positive-count-weighted mixture, sample one positive and four displayed negatives for each user in vectorized arrays, score all five rows, and pair the positive with the highest-scoring sampled negative. Optimize the BPR softplus loss plus a 0.2 pointwise-log-loss stabilizer. Stop gradients through the discrete negative selection and backpropagate only through the selected pair using the existing FM scorer, gradient accumulation, and Adam state. Limit training to roughly one selected pair per original training row per epoch and compare four-way hard sampling against one-way random BPR; reject the mechanism if runtime exceeds 180 seconds or the paired validation criterion is not met."}, "diagnosis": {"bottleneck": "The FM's pointwise log-loss is mismatched to the within-user ranking metrics, leaving relative positive-versus-negative ordering under-optimized.", "evidence": "The running-best primary has plateaued at 0.59610, with only 0.00036 improvement over the last three iterations, while the current FM still optimizes independent row probabilities rather than GAUC and nDCG ordering within each user. This suggests further tuning of the same pointwise setup has limited headroom.", "confidence": 0.78, "component": "loss_function", "edit_radius": "small", "expected_cost": "A localized baseline.py change implementing vectorized within-user BPR negative pairing or sampled listwise softmax, followed by validation of sampling ratio and loss mixing; feasible on one CPU within the runtime budget.", "incompatibilities": ["Keeping pure pointwise log-loss as the sole training objective", "Generating all positive-negative pairs per user, which would exceed the runtime budget"], "uncertainty": 0.28, "audit_concerns": ["test_label_access: ysel is read from enc[select_on] and passed to evaluate; if select_on can be 'test', this accesses test labels, and the diff does not constrain select_on to a label-available split."]}, "per_seed_primary": {"0": 0.5773379802703857, "1": 0.5744004845619202, "2": 0.5764849781990051}, "per_seed_gauc": {"0": 0.6391344666481018, "1": 0.6342355012893677, "2": 0.6378245949745178}, "per_seed_ndcg5": {"0": 0.5155414938926697, "1": 0.5145654678344727, "2": 0.5151453614234924}, "mean_delta": -0.025242375038247354, "p_positive": 0.0, "lower_95": -0.02722992393366379, "fix_attempts": 0, "wallclock_used_s": 0.0, "per_user_by_seed": {"0": {"4": 1.0, "15": 0.443426, "16": 1.0, "21": 0.340338, "23": 0.5, "25": 0.70542, "27": 0.679764, "29": 0.583333, "35": 1.0, "36": 1.0, "39": 1.0, "41": 0.596713, "45": 0.70986, "46": 0.698438, "49": 0.629737, "50": 0.716014, "53": 0.425965, "54": 1.0, "55": 0.737672, "57": 1.0, "58": 0.851064, "60": 0.315465, "64": 0.448661, "65": 0.527838, "67": 1.0, "68": 0.443426, "71": 0.5, "73": 0.76384, "74": 1.0, "75": 0.817067, "79": 1.0, "81": 0.493007, "82": 0.616414, "83": 1.0, "84": 0.315465, "94": 1.0, "95": 1.0, "97": 1.0, "98": 1.0, "99": 0.565465, "102": 0.95, "110": 0.699748, "111": 0.34632, "112": 0.25, "113": 1.0, "114": 0.64879