{"iter": 7, "id": "c33137d7", "parent_id": "bbe18131", "operation": "improve", "status": "closed", "evidence_type": "not_significant", "code_dir": "C:\\Users\\Ray\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\candidate_c33137d7", "hypothesis": {"mechanism": "Because the primary metric combines GAUC with a top-five list metric, a sampled within-user listwise objective that assigns probability mass jointly to all positives in a small candidate slate should better model competition near the top of each user's ranking than independent log-loss or uniformly weighted pairs.", "success_criterion_paired": "Primary on val-tier-2 improves by at least +0.0020 over the parent node's primary on val-tier-2, with both GAUC and nDCG@5 having nonnegative candidate-minus-parent deltas on that same tier.", "implementation_sketch": "Edit baseline.py only. Add a sampled-list training mode to run_fm using the same precomputed user-sorted label pools. In each vectorized minibatch, sample users from a 50% uniform and 50% positive-count-weighted mixture, then construct fixed slates containing up to two sampled positives and six sampled negatives per user, using replacement where a pool is smaller. Score the flattened slate with the existing FM, reshape to batch-by-eight, subtract each row maximum, and compute a multi-positive loss equal to negative log of the summed softmax probability assigned to positive slots. Derive the slate score gradient as softmax over all slots minus softmax restricted to positive slots, flatten it, and feed it through the existing vectorized FM gradient and Adam update. Mix this listwise loss at weight 0.7 with weight 0.3 of the current pointwise logistic loss, use approximately one slate per eligible-user draw per epoch rather than full user lists, and keep inference unchanged."}, "diagnosis": {"bottleneck": "The FM's pointwise log-loss is mismatched to the within-user ranking metrics, leaving relative positive-versus-negative ordering under-optimized.", "evidence": "The running-best primary has plateaued at 0.59610, with only 0.00036 improvement over the last three iterations, while the current FM still optimizes independent row probabilities rather than GAUC and nDCG ordering within each user. This suggests further tuning of the same pointwise setup has limited headroom.", "confidence": 0.78, "component": "loss_function", "edit_radius": "small", "expected_cost": "A localized baseline.py change implementing vectorized within-user BPR negative pairing or sampled listwise softmax, followed by validation of sampling ratio and loss mixing; feasible on one CPU within the runtime budget.", "incompatibilities": ["Keeping pure pointwise log-loss as the sole training objective", "Generating all positive-negative pairs per user, which would exceed the runtime budget"], "uncertainty": 0.28}, "per_seed_primary": {"0": 0.5874993205070496, "1": 0.5883194208145142, "2": 0.5877419710159302}, "per_seed_gauc": {"0": 0.6539181470870972, "1": 0.6551010012626648, "2": 0.6549224853515625}, "per_seed_ndcg5": {"0": 0.521080493927002, "1": 0.5215378999710083, "2": 0.5205615162849426}, "mean_delta": -0.01020477271892785, "p_positive": 0.0, "lower_95": -0.011659177284131938, "fix_attempts": 0, "wallclock_used_s": 0.0, "per_user_by_seed": {"0": {"4": 1.0, "15": 0.443426, "16": 1.0, "21": 0.690465, "23": 0.5, "25": 0.551573, "27": 0.768851, "29": 0.732132, "35": 1.0, "36": 0.83486, "39": 1.0, "41": 0.45046, "45": 0.70986, "46": 0.639942, "49": 0.928178, "50": 0.716014, "53": 0.354911, "54": 1.0, "55": 0.63796, "57": 1.0, "58": 1.0, "60": 1.0, "64": 0.720599, "65": 0.443426, "67": 1.0, "68": 1.0, "71": 0.340338, "73": 0.682197, "74": 1.0, "75": 0.817067, "79": 1.0, "81": 0.726966, "82": 0.786346, "83": 1.0, "84": 0.315465, "94": 1.0, "95": 1.0, "97": 1.0, "98": 0.565465, "99": 1.0, "102": 0.814466, "110": 0.699748, "111": 0.479141, "112": 0.565465, "113": 0.57546, "114": 0.648798, "118": 0.900401, "121": 0.778514, "122": 0.776966, "124": 0.478692, "125": 0.636397, "127": 1.0